@host = http://localhost:5109
@dealershipId = 1a0b0000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d
@oilChangeId = 3c2b0d50-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@evBatteryCheckId = 3c2b0d50-0000-4000-8000-000000000007

### Liveness probe
GET {{host}}/health/live

### Readiness probe — actually queries the database
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### OpenAPI document (also browsable via the Scalar UI at {{host}}/scalar/v1)
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json

### Availability — a seeded weekday, oil change (picks Alina, the narrowest-skilled free technician)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/availability?dealershipId={{dealershipId}}&serviceTypeId={{oilChangeId}}&date=2026-03-02

### Availability — closed day (Sunday): 200 with opensAtUtc null and no slots
GET {{host}}/api/v1/availability?dealershipId={{dealershipId}}&serviceTypeId={{oilChangeId}}&date=2026-03-01

### Availability — Saturday, EV battery check: only the 09:00 slot fits the 09:00-13:00 window
GET {{host}}/api/v1/availability?dealershipId={{dealershipId}}&serviceTypeId={{evBatteryCheckId}}&date=2026-03-07

### Availability — unknown dealership: 404
GET {{host}}/api/v1/availability?dealershipId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000&serviceTypeId={{oilChangeId}}&date=2026-03-02

### Book an appointment — pick a startsAtUtc from the availability response above, and real
### customer/vehicle ids from the demo data (see Demo/0201_CustomersAndVehicles.sql)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: sample-key-001

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealershipId}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChangeId}}",
  "vehicleId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "customerId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "startsAtUtc": "2026-03-02T09:00:00+00:00"
}

### Book an appointment — malformed body (empty dealershipId): 400 ValidationProblemDetails
POST {{host}}/api/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChangeId}}",
  "vehicleId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "customerId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "startsAtUtc": "2026-03-02T09:00:00+00:00"
}

### Book the same slot again — 409 with correlationId in both the response header and the
### problem body. Run the "Book an appointment" request above first so the slot is already taken,
### then send this one; the X-Correlation-Id header and the JSON body's correlationId extension match.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: demo-conflict-001

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealershipId}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChangeId}}",
  "vehicleId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "customerId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "startsAtUtc": "2026-03-02T09:00:00+00:00"
}
